client: when the server gives up on a file, drop its fragments

Fragments of a transfer the server abandons stayed in the channel's incoming
list until Netchan_Clear at the next map or disconnect. With 0002 each is
small, but a client that sat through several failed transfers on a long map
still kept every one of them.

--- a/engine/client/cl_parse.c
+++ b/engine/client/cl_parse.c
@@ -837,6 +837,10 @@
 void CL_ParseFileTransferFailed( sizebuf_t *msg )
 {
 	const char	*name = MSG_ReadString( msg );
+
+	// whatever had arrived of it is not going to be completed; give the memory back now
+	// rather than at the next map, when a fixed heap may already have run out
+	Netchan_DropIncoming( &cls.netchan, FRAG_FILE_STREAM );
 
 	if( !cls.demoplayback )
 		CL_ProcessFile( false, name );
